(1) THE EXCITATION SPECTRUM -- the Bogoliubov/phonon class
  The EOS carries ONE velocity scale: c_s^2 = dP/drho = sigma^2 = C/2
  (G233).  A coherent condensate's elementary branch is the acoustic
  (Goldstone) phonon  omega(k) = c_s k  -- GAUGELESS: the gap at k=0
  is EXACTLY ZERO (spontaneous coherence breaks the U(1) -> goldstone).
  The FULL Bogoliubov branch (healing term):  omega^2 = c_s^2 k^2 + (hbar k^2/2m)^2,
  i.e. omega = c_s k sqrt(1 + (k xi)^2/2) with the healing/coherence length xi = hbar/(sqrt(2) m c_s).

  coherence scales (m = 5.09 keV):
    MW     (c_s = 121.4 km/s):  healing xi  = 6.7673e-08 m = 2.1931e-24 pc
                         de Broglie     = 9.5705e-08 m
    cluster (c_s = 772 km/s):  healing xi  = 1.0652e-08 m
    -> xi/r_M < 2.15e-28 : the coherence scale is ~1e-7 m, far below EVERY observable scale

  THE BRANCH omega(k) at observable scales (MW well, c_s = 121.4 km/s):
           L [m]      k [1/m]    omega [1/s]    period [yr]  cycles in t_H
      1.9533e+20   3.2167e-20     3.9063e-15      5.097e+07        270.750
      3.1505e+20   1.9943e-20     2.4219e-15      8.221e+07        167.865
      3.0857e+21   2.0362e-21     2.4728e-16      8.052e+08         17.139
      3.0857e+22   2.0362e-22     2.4728e-17      8.052e+09          1.714
      3.0857e+23   2.0362e-23     2.4728e-18      8.052e+10          0.171
  wavelength completing ONE full cycle in t_H (omega t_H = 1): L_1 = 2 pi c_s t_H
    MW = 3.3229e+23 m = 10.77 Mpc;   cluster (c_s = 800 km/s) = 2.1890e+24 m = 70.9 Mpc
    -> modes ABOVE L_1 (~11 Mpc MW / ~71 Mpc clusters) are Hubble-SLOW (cycles << 1 in t_H);
       the well-to-Mpc modes oscillate on 50 Myr-8 Gyr timescales (the table above) but are
       NOT registered as observable propagating waves (G235 V2: no committed two-time/response
       function) -- the sector presents as STATIC ORDERED STRUCTURE: the envelope, exactly
       H047's 'frozen, no free degrees'.  The 2.55-keV LINE of the particle face (A05) has NO
       phonon counterpart: the condensate's only lines are acoustic, and at observable scales
       hbar*omega/(k_B T_b) ~ 1e-27 (well scale) - 1e-29 (Mpc scale): utterly classical, no
       quantum two-sided structure is testable (G235 V2).

  THE GAP STRUCTURE -- the committed linear response (G081):
    eigenproblem sigma^2 xi'' - (2 sigma^2/r) xi' + (2 sigma^2/r^2 - w^2) xi = 0,
    reduction xi = r u  ->  u'' = (w/sigma)^2 u  EXACT;
    fundamental:  omega^2 = w^2 = 0 EXACT (marginal), cap-invariant, zero-mode residual 1.8e-12.
  READING: the phase is RIGID at low k in the honest sense -- the k->0 branch is
    NEITHER growing (no Jeans instability: no fragmentation) NOR decaying (no damping:
    no heating/thermalization channel) NOR oscillating (no gapped mode).  A MASSIVE scalar
    counterpart would put a finite gap omega(0) = m_sc c^2/hbar at k = 0 and its mode would
    complete many cycles in t_H; the committed record has NO such mode: gap = 0, growth = 0.


(2) THE OBSERVABLE -- RESPONSE TO A BARYONIC PERTURBER (wake / phonons)
  Landau criterion (condensate with only the acoustic branch): v_c = min_p E(p)/p = c_s.
  v < c_s : NOTHING can be excited -- zero drag, zero dissipation, zero heating.
  v > c_s : a COHERENT wake (one macroscopic ordered mode, a Mach cone of the condensate).
  EITHER WAY the deposited energy is ORDERED (a collective mode), never stochastic heat.

  MACH numbers (velocity inputs are GENERIC, not committed):
                                    scenario         v [km/s]       c_s [km/s]       Mach v/c_s
                     MW well, passing galaxy            200.0            121.4             1.65
                        MW well, satellite              100.0            121.4             0.82
                       cluster core, merger            1500.0            771.0             1.95
                       Bullet sub (generic)            3000.0            771.0             3.89
  -> MW passages STRADDLE v_c (Mach 0.8-1.6); cluster merger shocks are supersonic (Mach 2-6)
     but deposit a COHERENT wake only.  The wake cannot thermalize: the dust's 2-body
     relaxation is t_relax = 1e73.0-1e75.9 x t_Hubble at 0.5-1 Mpc (G103) and the phantom's
     modes are collisionless collective states (marginal, omega^2 = 0 : no damping channel).

  ACOUSTIC RESPONSE TIMES:  t_ac = r_well/c_s  (the committed c_s t_ff/r = 1/sqrt(2) face, G127)
    MW well (r_break = 6.33 kpc, c_s = 121 km/s):  t_ac = 1.608e+15 s = 51.0 Myr
    cluster well (cap ~ 627 kpc, c_s = 800 km/s):  t_ac = 2.418e+16 s = 0.77 Gyr
    a merger perturber crossing ~1 Mpc at ~3000 km/s takes t_cross = 1.0e+16 s = 326 Myr
    -> t_cross << t_ac(cluster): the phantom sees the perturber as a QUASI-STATIC external
       potential (adiabatic): the response is the smooth gravitational wake -- the ordered
       kinematics -- NOT shock heating.  T_b = m sigma^2/k_B is fixed by the equilibrium, not
       raised by passages.

  ENERGY LEDGER (the no-heating prediction's number):
    phantom thermal content   (3/2) N_ph k_B T_b = 3.080e+51 J
    -> raising the phantom's sigma^2 by 1% (T -> 1.01 T_b) would need 3.080e+49 J
    generic cluster ICM shock energy (M_gas = 1.4e13 Msun, kT = 6 keV, FLAGGED generic) = 4.001e+55 J
    -> the shock carries 1.3e+06 x the phantom's 1%-heating cost -- and the coupling channels
       are dead (Landau gate + G103 collisionless).  The OBSERVED consequence:
       the G110 Bullet shows the dark peaks passing through with the 8-sigma galaxy/plasma
       offset (209/194 kpc) and NO dark-sector heating beyond the ordered kinematics; the G103
       timescales (1e73-1e76 t_H) certify the dust cannot heat itself.   The sector's velocity
       dispersion stays at sigma^2 = C/2 = the equilibrium value: mergers re-ORDER, they don't heat.


(3) THE GRANULARITY TEST -- smoothness below the coherence length
  A coherent phase has NO local density fluctuations below xi:
    MW phantom at r_M:  rho = 3.5430e-22 kg/m^3,  n = 3.9047e+10 m^-3;
    BEC-degeneracy criterion  n lambda_db^3 = 3.4228e-11  -- 20 orders BELOW 1:
      THE HONEST CAVEAT: the phantom is NOT a conventional degenerate Bose-Einstein
      condensate (macroscopic occupation of the single-particle ground state FAILS by ~1e11).
      Its 'coherence' is the G235 type-I reading: N_ph = 1.56e73 in ONE mode (lambda_fs = 0,
      R(k) = 1), floored by the finite-T Maxwellian at T_b = 9.52 K (v_rms = 210 km/s).  The
      no-free-streaming / smoothness signature survives: it is the share of BOTH type-I and
      type-III readings (G235 V1), and it is what the census tests.

    OBSERVABLE SMOOTHNESS: at every scale above ~1e-7 m the phantom density is the smooth
      A/r^2 envelope with ZERO substructure: one mode, marginal (omega^2 = 0) stability ->
      no Jeans instability, no fragmentation, no phantom subhalos.  The coherent-state
      fractional fluctuation is 1/sqrt(N_ph) = 2.55e-37 -- total suppression of shot noise.
      Contrast: CDM granularity (subhalos ~1e-3 of the host, ~1e5-1e6 Msun at the MW) and
      the WDM-relic truncation at M_hm = 5e5-5.8e6 Msun (G115).

    THE CENSUS CONFRONTATION (G215): the MW sub-1e6 counts resolve the RAR >1e5-class:
      N_obs = 19, LF rising steeply with NO break, against the relic-truncated predictions
      of 5.1 (5.7 keV) / 1.0 (3.3 keV)  ->  3.2-4.1 sigma lean to the SMOOTH (no-cutoff) face.
      The condensate predicts the SAME: R(k) = 1, lambda_fs = 0, no break at any scale.
      HONEST LIMITS: (i) the census is dominated by the FREE DUST (79-97% of dark, G110) --
      the granularity test isolates the phantom ENVELOPE, not the sector's subhalos;
      (ii) the phantom exists only inside its cap (0.62 r_M MW; 296-958 kpc clusters):
      outside, the dust alone carries the mass; (iii) the observable distinctive handle is
      the ENVELOPE's smoothness/slope (-2 vs NFW -3, H036) at 0.5-2 Mpc, not the subhalos.


(4) VERDICTS
  V1_the_mode_spectrum:
    THE GOLDSTONE PHONON, GAP AND GROWTH EXACTLY ZERO: the phantom's excitation spectrum is the acoustic branch omega(k) = c_s k with c_s^2 = C/2 = sigma^2 (c_s = 121.4 km/s MW; 628-915 km/s clusters, G127), the ONLY committed velocity scale (G233 EOS).
    The gap is EXACTLY ZERO (spontaneous coherence -> gapless; the committed linear-response spectrum G081 is omega^2 = 0 EXACT, marginal homology xi = c1 r + c2 r^2, reduction u'' = (w/sigma)^2 u -- the weak-field k->0 limit of the same rigidity).
    The mode structure's observable content: (a) NO growing mode (no Jeans instability -> the phase cannot fragment), (b) NO decaying mode (no damping channel -> nothing can heat it), (c) Hubble-SLOW long-wavelength modes: a mode completes one cycle in t_H only at L_1 = 2 pi c_s t_H = 10.8 Mpc (MW; 70.9 Mpc at cluster c_s = 800 km/s), so at every envelope-observable scale the modes present as the STATIC ORDERED ENVELOPE -- exactly H047's 'frozen, no free degrees' (the well-to-Mpc modes oscillate on 50 Myr-8 Gyr timescales but no propagating-wave observable is committed: no two-time/response function, G235 V2).
    The healing/de Broglie coherence scale is xi ~ 6.77e-08 m / lambda_db ~ 9.57e-08 m (MW) -- 20+ orders below any observable scale.

  V2_the_no_heating_prediction:
    ZERO STOCHASTIC HEATING, BY TWO INDEPENDENT GATES: (i) the Landau criterion -- v_c = min_p E(p)/p = c_s, so subsonic passages excite NOTHING and supersonic passages emit only a COHERENT (one-mode, ordered) wake: neither deposits stochastic energy; (ii) the collisionless cert (G103): the dust's 2-body relaxation is t_relax = 1e73.0-1e75.9 x t_Hubble at 0.5-1 Mpc, and the phantom's modes are marginal (omega^2 = 0) -- no channel exists to turn wake energy into heat on ANY timescale.
    A generic cluster ICM shock carries ~1e6 x the phantom's 1%-sigma^2 heating cost, and the sector's temperature STAYS at the equilibrium T_b = m sigma^2/k_B (9.52 K at the 5.00 keV bookkeeping mass; 9.69 K at the committed 5.09 keV) -- a fixed point (sigma^2 = C/2), not an input.
    OBSERVED: merging clusters show NO tidal heating of the dark sector beyond ordered kinematics -- the G110 Bullet (dark peaks pass through, 8-sigma galaxy/plasma offset, dust on the galaxies at 209/194 kpc, phantom capped away from the cores) and the G103 timescales; the mergers re-ORDER, they do not heat.
    A positive detection of dark-sector thermalization (broadened dispersion / heated envelope in a merger) WOULD KILL this face.

  V3_honest_statement:
    THE CONDENSATE FACE'S TESTABLE CORE: the phantom's dark sector is a collective-moded phase whose observables are SMOOTHNESS (no density fluctuations below xi ~ 1e-7 m; one mode, R(k) = 1, lambda_fs = 0; no phantom substructure -- envelope slope -2 vs NFW -3, H036), NO-LOCAL-HEATING (Landau v_c = c_s + G103 collisionless 1e73-1e76 t_H; the Bullet's ordered offset with no thermalization; T_b fixed at the equilibrium m sigma^2/k_B, 9.52-9.69 K over the 5.00-5.09 keV bookkeeping band), and NO SHMF BREAK (G215: 19 objects at the LF rising, no truncation -- the smooth face is the one already leaning at 3.2-4.1 sigma).
    WHAT WOULD SHOW COHERENCE: a smooth phantom envelope with zero substructure; no dark heating in mergers; a break-free sub-halo census.
    WHAT WOULD KILL IT: (a) granularity / phantom subhalos in the envelope; (b) any dark-sector thermalization signature (tidal heating beyond ordered kinematics); (c) a committed gapped or particle-like response chi(omega) -- the G235 V2 open FDT register: the condensate predicts an acoustic-pole chi(omega) with a single gapless sound branch and zero damping, a measured massive/gapped mode would falsify it; (d) phantom density structure below ~1e-7 m (unobservable -- the coherence scale is 1e-7 m, so the granularity test at astrophysical scales never reaches the coherence regime: smoothness is TOTAL, and total smoothness below observability cannot be over-tested).
    THE HONEST TENSION, REGISTERED: the phantom is NOT a conventional degenerate BEC (n lambda_db^3 = 3.4e-11 << 1 -- the occupancy test fails by ~1e11) and is only the CAPPED minority of the dark sector (dust share 79-97%, G110): 'the condensate' means the G235 type-I one-mode reading of the PHANTOM component (the baryon-sourced coherent envelope), not the collisionless free dust, and the granularity/no-heating tests discriminate that envelope's physics -- while the sector's subhalos remain the dust's CDM-like business.

